 2. 💰 Trump&#x27;s $2 billion giveback to seniors 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump promised a $2 billion handout to seniors late Friday night — checks to help pay Medicare premiums, just a month before the midterm election, Axios' Ben Berkowitz writes .

 Why it matters: Facing the worst economic polling for any president in a decade, and with the cost of living at the top of voters' minds, Trump is scrambling to put money directly in Americans' pockets. Trump said in a Truth Social post just before 11 p.m. ET: "I am pleased to announce that my Administration will, immediately, begin sending 'Checks' of nearly $100 to over 20 MILLION wonderful Seniors to help pay for their Medicare Part B premiums, which we have already reduced by significant amounts."

 The White House , in a fact sheet , said eligible seniors will receive a direct deposit of $90 in early October, or paper checks if they don't have direct deposit. The $90 represents less than half of one month's Part B premium . Follow the money: It's the latest in a long series of checks offered by the president, including:

 $5,000 for every adult citizen if Republicans win both the House and Senate in midterms — a $1 trillion+ pledge he made in September and reiterated last night. The White House branded it the "Trump Dividend." $500 Obamacare rebates for more than 1 million people who were purportedly overcharged for their benefits. (Those checks began going out this week.) A "dividend" of some kind for those living near data centers. Those pledges come on top of rebates he proposed in 2025 that were not ultimately paid, including tariff rebates and DOGE dividends.

