 3. 🪖 Scoop: Secret Camp David huddle 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Vice President Vance. Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photos: Brandon Bell and U.S. Navy via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump's top cabinet members huddled for hours at Camp David yesterday to discuss next steps in the Iran war and the Saudi-Houthi conflict in Yemen, three U.S. officials told Axios' Barak Ravid. 

 Why it matters: The highly unusual meeting wasn't announced by the Trump administration. The last time a similar meeting took place was in June 2025, just days before Israel went to war against Iran. 🔎 Behind the scenes: Vice President Vance chaired the meeting, the officials said.

 Among the other participants: Secretary of State Marco Rubio, Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth, White House envoy Steve Witkoff, CIA director John Ratcliffe and chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff Gen. Dan Caine. "Things were decided or at least deeply discussed," one of the officials said, referring to the crisis in the Middle East.

 The White House declined to comment. The big picture: With negotiations stalled, President Trump is considering resuming major combat operations in Iran.

 Yesterday afternoon, while his advisers were at Camp David, Trump was asked by reporters what his next move on Iran will be. "If I told you, you would have a major story," he said. "But you will see. It is working out very well. Iran is not doing well." Share this story . 

 
 
