 7. 🧊 Stat du jour: Record Swiss thaw 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Glaciologist Matthias Huss holds a pole that indicates 4 meters of ice lost over the past year on the Scex Rouge glacier in Les Diablerets, Switzerland. Photo: Denis Balibouse/Reuters A record-shattering European heat wave accelerated the shrinking of Swiss glaciers this year: The country's glaciers shed more than 5% of their ice in 2026, according to a report from Swiss monitoring groups.

 Zoom out: Swiss glaciers have ⁠lost almost a fifth of their ice in the last five years, threatening future water supplies, Reuters reports. Keep reading . 

 
 
