 8. 📸 1 for the road: 56 Trumps 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Image : TIME As of this week, President Trump has appeared on the cover of TIME more than anyone else. Here are all 56, spanning 37 years — ending with the latest , which surpassed 55 covers featuring Richard Nixon, the champ for a half-century. 

 The first, which has hung above a urinal at Mar-a-Lago, ran on Jan. 16, 1989, when Trump was 42 and personified that era's aspiration for luxury. TIME notes that his voice in that story remains familiar: "I have an absolute strategy, but it's an innate strategy and not definable ... When you start studying yourself too deeply, you start seeing things that maybe you don't want to see." 🥁 Trump told TIME for this week's cover story that he liked 17 of his first 55 covers.

